    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 2:01 · the wall</span>
      <strong>MAKE THE LARGE BRICK ON TOP STICK OUT</strong>
      The stone wall under the flowering vine carries the room's most explicit instruction, printed across the middle of the screen: <b>MAKE THE LARGE BRICK ON TOP STICK OUT, THEN TOUCH IT. THE REQUIRED BRICK WILL APPEAR, TOUCH IT TO DISMANTLE IT.</b> Push a brick proud of the face and touch it; the wall answers by showing you the one it actually wants. Touch that and it comes away. No numbers, no order to memorise — just the correct brick, twice.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l10-brick-puzzle.jpg" alt="The dry-stone wall in Garden under a pink flowering vine, with the brick dismantle instruction on screen" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
